<tr><td colspan=4><font size=2 face=verdana color=#ffffff>His world is a garden.  Life is based on the Harmony of nature, any discord within nature is abhorrent to him.  Walking in beauty and living in harmony are what is important to him.  Irregularities must be corrected. 


“Help!” The young druid heard as he strolled through the Forrest on the cool autumn night.  “HELP! Help, HELP!”  “I come!” he thought into the into the wind,  “I come.”  Without thought, he became one with his restless heart.  His blood heated as he began his change, elements becoming clearer and distinct, becoming himself letting the world know his nature…  “I am a WOLF!”

A deep howl escaped his lips as his muscles bunched, a warning to enemies, and promise to his pack;  “I come!  With me I bring death!”   “Hold on my brother I come to help! “  Effortlessly he ran, a fast lope, letting instinct guide his path to danger, bringing hope.

Nearing the treeline he slowed.  His nose brought him the scent of dwarf and the overpowering, sickening scent of cyclops.  Another howling bay he issued, announcing his arrival, calling on nature, and praying to Karana to help him this day.   

“First health then fire I give freely.”  He thought to himself as he gathered his will.  Releasing healing on the dwarf, he snarled at the cyclops.  “You are mine!  I am your nightmare in the flesh, It is time to sleep” Backing slowly he cast his first spell.  The cyclops slowed but kept coming, which suited the wolf well.   A swarm of lights seemed to surround the brutish cyclops causing pain and anguish as it felt the thousands stings upon itself.   Closer and closer the cyclops came, and the young wolf decided to let it learn a new and final  lesson in pain. Fire.  And more Fire. Hammering blows of heat and flame pounding it and driving it down.  A vision from hell could not be milder as the giant cyclops fell.

Back to the dwarf ran the druid to ensure all was well.  “Let me share my wolf spirit with you earth brother, and we will get you to safety until our paths cross again”.
